menu "dgx-ui"

config DGX_UI_HATCH
    bool "A hatched fill on a screen of 1 bit: DGX_UI_HATCH in the table of colours"
    default y if DGX_ENABLE_V_BW_SCREEN || DGX_ENABLE_ST7920
    default n
    help
        The looks fill with a pixel through a pixel, (x + y) & 1 of the screen, where the table of the
        painter's colours holds DGX_UI_HATCH: the dim fill of a monochrome screen. On by itself with the
        drivers of 1-bit panels of DGX (SSD1306, SSD1309, SH1106, ST7565R, ST7920); a program that draws on
        a 1-bit virtual screen of its own turns it on. Off, a program carries none of it.

endmenu
